# Ctrl+G and Ctrl+L: MainV2.ProcessCmdKey's `new SerialOutputNMEA().Show()` and `new
# SpectrogramUI().Show()` (MainV2.cs:4124-4130, 4138-4145) - the windows CONFIG > Advanced's NMEA
# and Spectrogram buttons open (ConfigAdvanced.cs:47-50, 119-122; config-nmea.gui and
# config-spectrogram.gui test them there), opened here by the key over any screen
# (crates/mp-gui/src/cmd_keys.rs).
#
# The claim: Ctrl+G on the flight screen shows the NMEA output as the button opens it - Connect,
# 5hz, 4800 - over that screen; its close box puts it away. Ctrl+L shows the spectrogram, ACC1,
# -80 to -20, nothing loaded, over the flight screen and then over the planning screen. On SETUP,
# which draws the Advanced page's windows itself, Ctrl+G's window shows once, as there.
#
# No vehicle. Run from the repository root:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/keys-nmea-spectrogram.gui
#
# Not yet run: the budget is a guess, set by hand until a passing run records one.
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 10

expect config.nmea.window false
expect config.spectrogram.window false

# Ctrl+G over the flight screen.
key ctrl+g
expect screen fly
expect config.nmea.window true
expect config.nmea.opened 1
expect config.nmea.button Connect
expect config.nmea.ratetext 5hz
expect config.nmea.baud 4800
click nmea-close
expect config.nmea.window false

# Ctrl+L over the flight screen, then over the planning screen.
key ctrl+l
expect config.spectrogram.window true
expect config.spectrogram.opened 1
expect config.spectrogram.sensor ACC1
expect config.spectrogram.min -80
expect config.spectrogram.max -20
expect config.spectrogram.log none
click spect-close
expect config.spectrogram.window false
click tab-plan
expect screen plan
key ctrl+l
expect config.spectrogram.window true
expect config.spectrogram.opened 2
click spect-close
expect config.spectrogram.window false

# Over SETUP, which draws the Advanced page's windows: the same window, once.
click tab-setup
expect screen setup
key ctrl+g
expect config.nmea.window true
expect config.nmea.opened 2
click nmea-close
expect config.nmea.window false
